---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Scavland Weapons Database & Attachments Guide — Scavland Wiki" description="Complete weapon catalog for Scavland: 25+ firearms, 300+ attachment modifications, calibers, recoil handling, and weapon durability systems." keywords="Scavland weapons, Scavland attachments, firearms database, gun modification, ammo calibers, Scavland wiki" canonical="/weapons/">
  <article class="article-layout">
    <header class="guide-header">
      <div class="meta-row">
        <span class="badge official">ARSENAL DATABASE</span>
        <time datetime="2026-08-31">Updated August 31, 2026</time>
      </div>
      <h1>Scavland Weapons &amp; Attachments Database</h1>
      <p class="lede">Explore the verified firearm roster of Zalesye: 25+ distinct firearms, 300+ modular attachments, caliber ballistics, and tactical maintenance.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="note" style="margin-bottom:2rem;background:var(--card-bg,#161616);border:1px solid var(--border-color,#333);padding:1.25rem;border-radius:8px;">
      <h3 style="margin:0 0 0.5rem 0;color:var(--accent,#ffaa00);">Weapon Mechanics Summary</h3>
      <p style="margin:0;line-height:1.6;color:var(--text-muted,#ccc);">Weapons in Scavland feature persistent degradation, caliber matching, modular attachment rails (optics, muzzle brakes, suppressors, foregrips, magazines), and jam chances under low durability.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Weapon Categories in Scavland</h2>
      
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1.5rem 0;">
        <div style="background:var(--card-bg,#161616);border:1px solid var(--border-color,#333);padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;color:#fff;">Pistols &amp; Sidearms</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted,#aaa);margin:0;">Compact 9x18mm / 9x19mm handguns. Lightweight, high mobility, essential backup when primary weapons jam in close-quarters bunker combat.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--card-bg,#161616);border:1px solid var(--border-color,#333);padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;color:#fff;">Submachine Guns (SMGs)</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted,#aaa);margin:0;">High rate-of-fire compact automatics. Devastating against mutant swarms and unarmored stalkers, but burn through ammo quickly.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--card-bg,#161616);border:1px solid var(--border-color,#333);padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;color:#fff;">Assault &amp; Battle Rifles</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted,#aaa);margin:0;">Standard 5.45x39mm and 7.62x39mm rifles. The backbone of wasteland survival. Modular rails accept scopes, tactical flashlights, and suppressors.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--card-bg,#161616);border:1px solid var(--border-color,#333);padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;color:#fff;">Shotguns</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted,#aaa);margin:0;">12-gauge pump-action and double-barrel shotguns. Invaluable for bunker corridor clearing against aggressive subterranean mutants.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--card-bg,#161616);border:1px solid var(--border-color,#333);padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;color:#fff;">Sniper &amp; Marksman Rifles</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted,#aaa);margin:0;">High-caliber 7.62x54mmR bolt-action and semi-auto rifles. Built for long-range target elimination across open marshlands.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--card-bg,#161616);border:1px solid var(--border-color,#333);padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;color:#fff;">Crafted &amp; Scavenged Improvised Guns</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted,#aaa);margin:0;">Pipe weapons and converted tools crafted from scrap metal and springs. Cheap and readily replaceable for initial wasteland runs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>300+ Attachment Customization System</h2>
      <p>Every firearm in Scavland features multiple modular attachment slots:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Muzzle Devices:</strong> Compensators (reduce vertical recoil), flash hiders (conceal night flash), and suppressors (drastically reduce noise radius to avoid alerting nearby mutant packs).</li>
        <li><strong>Optics &amp; Sights:</strong> Iron sights, red dot reflex sights, holo scopes, and variable zoom telescopic lenses.</li>
        <li><strong>Grips &amp; Handguards:</strong> Angled foregrips for weapon stability, tactical lasers for hip-fire accuracy, and flashlight modules for dark underground vaults.</li>
        <li><strong>Magazines &amp; Drums:</strong> Extended capacity magazines, quick-draw clips, and drum mags that alter reload speed and weight balance.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Weapon Maintenance &amp; Cleaning</h2>
      <p>Firing weapons in rain, swamp mud, or the toxic Mist rapidly degrades condition. Keeping weapon cleaning kits and gun oil in your safehouse stash ensures your guns won't jam during critical gunfights.</p>
    </div>

    <footer class="guide-footer" style="margin-top:3rem;padding-top:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border-color,#333);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;">
      <a class="button secondary" href="/factions/">10 Factions Guide →</a>
      <a class="button" href="/guide/scavland-beginner-guide/">Read Beginner Guide →</a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>
